{"name":"Veiled Chameleon","hex":"#80b690","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"veiled chameleon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A species of arboreal chameleon with a prominent casque on its head, Chamaeleo calyptratus, native to the south-western Arabian Peninsula."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/veiled_chameleon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Veiled chameleon","blocks":[{"text":"The veiled chameleon is a species of chameleon native to the Arabian Peninsula in Yemen and Saudi Arabia. Other common names include cone-head chameleon, Yemen chameleon, and Yemeni chameleon. They are born pastel green and without their distinctive casques on their head. When newly hatched veiled chameleons are surprised, they may drop to the ground and turn a bright red color due to stress."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Yemen_Chameleon.jpg/330px-Yemen_Chameleon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Veiled_chameleon","wikidata":"Q1124882"},{"title":"Chameleon","blocks":[{"text":"Chameleons are a distinctive and highly specialized clade of Old World lizards with 200 species described as of June 2015. The members of this family are best known for their distinct range of colours, being capable of colour-shifting camouflage. The large number of species in the family exhibit considerable variability in their capacity to change colour. For some, it is more of a shift of brightness ; for others, a plethora of colour-combinations can be seen."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Panther_Chameleon_738367_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Panther_Chameleon_738367_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chameleon","wikidata":"Q37686"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Chamaeleo_calyptratus_distribution.png/500px-Chamaeleo_calyptratus_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Chamaeleo_calyptratus_distribution.png/500px-Chamaeleo_calyptratus_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChamaeleo_calyptratus_distribution.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Chamaeleo_calyptratus_-_AMNH_-_DSC06272.JPG/500px-Chamaeleo_calyptratus_-_AMNH_-_DSC06272.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Chamaeleo_calyptratus_-_AMNH_-_DSC06272.JPG/1280px-Chamaeleo_calyptratus_-_AMNH_-_DSC06272.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Chamaeleo_calyptratus_-_AMNH_-_DSC06272.JPG/500px-Chamaeleo_calyptratus_-_AMNH_-_DSC06272.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Skeleton","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChamaeleo_calyptratus_-_AMNH_-_DSC06272.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/C_Calyptratus_female.jpg/120px-C_Calyptratus_female.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/C_Calyptratus_female.jpg/250px-C_Calyptratus_female.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/C_Calyptratus_female.jpg/120px-C_Calyptratus_female.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AC_Calyptratus_female.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Jemencham%C3%A4leon_Chamaeleo_ca